# Style layer audit (web)

When the user asks for a **style audit**, **theming cleanup**, **dedupe styles**, or **CSS token pass** in the web app:

1. Follow **`Docs/CURSOR_STYLE_LAYER_AUDIT.md`** (Phase 1 prompt, then Phase 2 checklist, Phase 3 verify).
2. **Layers for this repo:** tokens in `apps/web/src/index.css`; cross-feature presets in `apps/web/src/components/styles.ts`; feature-only in `apps/web/src/features/<feature>/styles.ts`.
3. Prefer **semantic CSS variables** for repeated colors/states; use **TS style modules** for composed `className` strings shared across components.
4. After edits, run **`pnpm turbo lint typecheck test`** (or `pnpm --filter @questlog/web` equivalents if scoped).

Do not redesign visuals unless the user asks; focus on boundaries, deduplication, and tokenization.
